6. Trade-offs → What did we gain and what did we sacrifice?
Gain: availability
Temporary failure:
request → failure
           ↓
         retry
           ↓
        success
The user never notices the transient failure.
________________________________________
Gain: resilience
A dependency can briefly disappear without immediately causing every upstream request to fail.
________________________________________
Sacrifice: additional load
Every retry is another request.
If:
1M requests
and 20% retry:
1M + 200K
requests reach the system.
________________________________________
Sacrifice: latency
Without retry:
100 ms
With retry:
100 ms
+
backoff
+
100 ms
Potentially much slower.
________________________________________
Sacrifice: correctness complexity
For reads:
GET /user/123
retrying is usually relatively safe.
For writes:
POST /payment
POST /order
POST /transfer
retrying can create duplicate side effects.
Therefore:
Retries are much easier for idempotent operations than non-idempotent operations.
